       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem. 2000 mg is 10 times the maximum daily dose, and the patient's normal kidney and liver function, weight, and lack of allergies don't make it safe. I can't find a clinical scenario where a single daily dose that size would be appropriate.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **If the dose was a typo,** tell me the intended dose, such as 50 mg or 200 mg, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **If you really intend 2000 mg,** for example on a toxicology recommendation, the order needs to come from your attending or the supervising prescriber. They can enter it themselves or tell me to, with a documented rationale. A pharmacist will probably want to verify it as well.\n- **If the patient has already taken a large amount of sertraline,** that's an overdose. Please contact your team and poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) now."
      }
